    "url": "/region/calabria/#era-1806",
    "why": "All sources give 1806 for the change: Joseph Bonaparte entered Naples 15 Feb 1806 (crowned by Napoleon's act of 30 Mar); British troops held Calabria and won at Maida 4 Jul 1806; Massena had not pacified it until end of summer 1806; brigandage persisted under Murat. Ferdinand kept Sicily and never renounced the crown (rival claimant, British-backed). Contested for Calabria specifically."
