    "url": "/region/calabria/#era-1861",
    "why": "Garibaldi landed in Calabria 19 Aug 1860 and took Reggio 21 Aug (Expedition of the Thousand); plebiscite 21 Oct 1860 and annexation decree 17 Dec 1860 (Dickinson House Divided, citing Wambaugh); Gaeta capitulated 13 Feb 1861 and Civitella del Tronto 20 Mar 1861; Kingdom of Italy proclaimed 17 Mar 1861. The change of sovereignty ran Aug 1860 to Mar 1861. Allied landings at Reggio 3 Sep 1943 (Operation Baytown) were under the Italian armistice; sovereignty stayed with the Kingdom of Italy, so not treated as contested. FIX: 'Provincia di Vibo Valentia' is anachronistic for 1861-1995: law of 6 Mar 1992, effective 1 Jan 1996; before that Briatico was in Catanzaro province."
